1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.602
You're going to build a full multi-agent system

2
00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.471
that communicates using A2A

3
00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:07.073
over the course of the next seven lessons.

4
00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:09.776
You'll start simple with a single agent,

5
00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:11.778
then build out more agents and tie

6
00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.780
them together with A2A as we go,

7
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.982
using a variety of frameworks and models.

8
00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:19.586
This agentic system will focus on the healthcare industry,

9
00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.489
but the concepts will apply to any multi-agent system.

10
00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.691
You're going to access models through

11
00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:26.760
Vertex AI Model Garden on Google Cloud

12
00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.963
because it provides a convenient, secure, and scalable way

13
00:00:29.963 --> 00:00:31.931
to access many different models.

14
00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:35.435
But A2A can work on any cloud provider or even on prem.

15
00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.937
And don't worry if you're not familiar with Google Cloud.

16
00:00:38.138 --> 00:00:39.706
We've got everything set up for

17
00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.541
you in the DeepLearning.AI environment.

18
00:00:41.574 --> 00:00:44.344
In this lesson, you'll build an agent

19
00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.546
powered by Claude Haiku 4.5

20
00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.549
that answers questions about a health insurance policy.

21
00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.352
In the next lesson, you'll wrap it up as an A2A server

22
00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.354
with the A2A SDK.

23
00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.356
All right, let's code.

24
00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.659
First, I'll start by importing some libraries we'll be using,

25
00:00:59.659 --> 00:01:02.262
including the AnthropicVertex library

26
00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.664
to interact with Claude on Vertex AI.

27
00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.634
All of these should already be installed in this environment.

28
00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.236
Next, I'll run this load_dotenv method

29
00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.239
to set up some environment variable constants that we'll be using.

30
00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.676
Next, I'll use this helper function to authenticate

31
00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:19.679
the DeepLearning.AI environment to Google Cloud.

32
00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.881
You'll see this in all of the code samples today.

33
00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:23.883
If you want to run this locally, there are links

34
00:01:23.883 --> 00:01:25.985
to the Google Cloud docs at the end of

35
00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.088
the notebook, which explain how to set this up.

36
00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:31.391
Now, I'll create a client to access Claude.

37
00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:34.394
So we'll create an AnthropicVertex object

38
00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.196
and fill in the Google Cloud

39
00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:39.499
project_id, region, and our credentials.token.

40
00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:42.001
Claude on its own doesn't know anything

41
00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:44.204
about the insurance policy we're going to be talking about.

42
00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.706
So, you'll need to load in information

43
00:01:46.806 --> 00:01:48.775
from the policy docs to include in Claude's prompt.

44
00:01:49.075 --> 00:01:52.779
We're following a similar pattern to retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG.

45
00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:55.682
In this case, we're just loading the entire document

46
00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.284
into the prompt instead of chunking and retrieving.

47
00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:01.287
Next, I'll write out the user's prompt to the agent.

48
00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:04.491
In this case, how much would I pay for mental health therapy?

49
00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.593
Because mental health is important.

50
00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:09.195
Now, let's send all of this to Claude.

51
00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:12.098
I'll call client.messages.create

52
00:02:12.398 --> 00:02:15.301
and set the result to a variable called response.

53
00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:19.405
I'll say which model I want, in this case Claude Haiku 4.5

54
00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:21.608
I'll set max_tokens and

55
00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.843
provide a system prompt. This defines the persona

56
00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:26.412
and task that you want your agent to do.

57
00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.748
In this case, you are an expert

58
00:02:28.748 --> 00:02:31.384
insurance agent designed to assist with coverage queries.

59
00:02:31.384 --> 00:02:34.787
Use the provided documents to answer questions about insurance policies.

60
00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:36.956
If the information is not available in

61
00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:39.092
the documents, respond with I don't know.

62
00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:42.795
And then I'll pass in some messages, which include our PDF document

63
00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.597
and our user prompt from earlier.

64
00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:47.000
Now that I've sent a request to Claude,

65
00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:49.202
let's print out the response as markdown.

66
00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:51.905
Note, because of the way Jupyter notebooks print markdown,

67
00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:54.507
I have to escape the dollar sign characters

68
00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.809
to make this agent's responses appear clearly.

69
00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.712
And it looks like it'll cost me 10% In-Network

70
00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:01.514
and 30% Out-of-Network

71
00:03:01.514 --> 00:03:04.617
after I meet my $1,700 deductible.

72
00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.120
Let's look at the PDF and make sure this is right.

73
00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.823
and it is.

74
00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.527
Let's go back to the code. I'm going

75
00:03:14.527 --> 00:03:16.629
to wrap this up in a PolicyAgent class

76
00:03:16.729 --> 00:03:18.698
to make it easier to use in the next lesson.

77
00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:21.701
This will be saved in a file called agents.py

78
00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:24.604
with the help of this Jupyter magic function writefile.

79
00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.707
The actual procedure of the agent didn't change.

80
00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:34.480
So now I'll just import this new class, create an object,

81
00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.883
and call answer_query to get a response.

82
00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.586
And we got the same information as before.

83
00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:43.856
In the next lesson, we'll make this PolicyAgent A2A compliant.

84
00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.459
See you there.
